  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Beraprost is a vasodilator and platelet aggregation inhibitor, an antithrombotic agent investigated as a drug. It is not an approved medicine in major Western markets and remains investigational, though it has been used in some Asian countries for vascular disease such as pulmonary hypertension.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5977854\">Wikidata Q5977854</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>beraprost</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>B01AC19</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB05229\">DB05229</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/23663404\">23663404</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:135633\">135633</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5977854\">Q5977854</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C24H29NaO5</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>420.481 g/mol (PubChem CID 23663404)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>3.2 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table><p><small>Drugs.Common 25.09 gave 398.5 g/mol (-5.2 %); replaced by the value above</small></p></body></html>"));
